    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener>
                    <dateline><date when="1946-12-10">December 10,
                        1946</date></dateline><salute>Dear <rs type="person"
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__1928">Dr. Tillich</rs>:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>Your secretary telephoned me yesterday to say that you had not received payment
                    for your review of <rs type="person" ref="#tillich_person_id__1683"
                        >Santayana</rs>&apos;s <q><rs ref="#tillich__7WZP2N3A" type="work">The Idea
                            of Christ in the Gospels</rs>.</q><note type="ea">Vgl. <rs type="person"
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__1928">Paul Tillich</rs>: <rs
                            ref="#tillich__SFFJNAI2" type="work">Christianity Without Paul</rs>
                        (1946).</note></p>
                <p>Your review appeared in our issue of <date when="1946-10-12">October 12</date>,
                    and we have in our office your cancelled check for it. The check amounted to
                    15.50$, and it has on it the stamp of the Union Theological Seminary besides
                    your personal endorsement.</p>
                <p>I hope that this information will straighten out your accounts.</p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>Sincerely yours,</salute>
                    <signed><hi rend="hand"><rs type="person" ref="#tillich_person_id__4825"
                                >Caroline Whiting</rs></hi><lb/> Assistant Literary Editor.</signed>
                </closer>

            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
